Austin, Texas-based Oracle Corporation ( ORCL )&nbsp;is a global technology company specializing in enterprise software, databases, and cloud computing.&nbsp;Valued at a market cap of&nbsp; $434.5 billion ,&nbsp;Oracle has built its business around its widely used database technology, while increasingly shifting its focus toward cloud infrastructure and AI-powered enterprise applications.

Companies with a market capitalization of $200 billion or more are typically referred to as "mega-cap stocks." ORCL fits right into that category, with its market cap exceeding this threshold, reflecting its substantial size and influence in the software infrastructure industry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

However, the stock currently trades 56.4% below its&nbsp; 52-week high of $345.72 &nbsp;recorded on Sep. 10, 2025. ORCL has&nbsp; declined 26% &nbsp;over the past three months, notably outperforming the S&P 500 Index ( $SPX ), which&nbsp; has rallied 2% .&nbsp;

The stock fell 37.2% over the past 52 weeks and 22.6% on a YTD basis, underperforming the index’s 18.6% rise and 12.7% rally over the same time frames.&nbsp;

ORCL has been trading below its 200-day moving average since mid-June and has recently climbed above its 50-day moving average.&nbsp;

Oracle has underperformed the broader market over the past year largely because investors have become increasingly concerned that the enormous cost of its AI infrastructure expansion could outweigh the near-term benefits of its strong cloud growth. Oracle raised $43 billion of debt in FY2026 and expects to raise roughly another $40 billion in FY2027, including a planned $20 billion equity issuance, to finance its AI data-center buildout. This has raised concerns about higher leverage, potential shareholder dilution and weaker free cash flow,

Compared with its rival, Palantir Technologies Inc. ( PLTR ) has&nbsp; grown 17.8% over the past year &nbsp;and 4.8% in 2026, outperforming ORCL.

Wall Street continues to favor the stock highly. Among the 44 analysts tracking ORCL, the overall consensus stands at a “ Strong Buy .” Its mean price target of $251.50 suggests 66.7% upside potential from current price levels.

